course: dictionary
lesson: 7804
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Quaver is one of them: it can name a musical note, describe a shaking voice, or mean the shake itself. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Counting puzzles are about beats: in 4/4 time a bar holds four crotchet beats, a minim lasts two beats and a quaver half a beat.» Beats, bar and crotchet are music words, so quaver here is a music note. A quaver lasts half a beat.
explain: Now read this: «Her voice quavered as she told the class about her lost dog.» Here quavered is a verb, and the voice shook because she was upset. The story tells you the feeling. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it, then test it in the sentence.
fact: A quaver is a musical note that lasts half a beat in common time.
fact: In the USA, a quaver is called an eighth note.
fact: Two quavers equal one crotchet.
fact: «Quavering» means shaking, often because someone is afraid, nervous, old or upset.
fact: «Quavers» is also a UK crisp brand, so check the context to see if it is about food or music.
exercise: In «two quavers equal one crotchet», how many quavers make one crotchet? | *Two | Eight | Half | Four
exercise: «Her voice quavered as she read the poem aloud.» What is her voice doing? | *Shaking, because she feels nervous | Stopping for a rest | Singing a very high note on purpose | Getting louder and louder
exercise: What is a quaver called in the USA? | Whole note | *Eighth note | Sixteenth note | Half note
test: «A minim lasts two beats and a quaver half a beat.» What does quaver mean here? | A shake in the voice | *A musical note that lasts half a beat | A brand of crisps | A loud noise
test: Which word means a shake or tremble in the voice? | beam | rest | *quaver | bar
exam: A quaver lasts half as long as a crotchet, so how long is a quaver compared with a crotchet? | Four times as long | *Half as long | Same length | Twice as long
